# Project Rules
MVC architecture, REST API
## General
- Use clean, readable, maintainable code
- Follow consistent naming conventions
- Avoid unnecessary comments
- Prefer simplicity over cleverness

---

## Frontend (React + TailwindCSS)

### React Rules
- Use functional components only
- Use hooks instead of class components
- Keep components small and reusable
- Move business logic into hooks or services
- Avoid inline functions inside JSX when possible

### Naming
- Components: PascalCase (UserCard.jsx)
- Functions: camelCase
- Variables: camelCase

### Structure
- components/: reusable UI
- pages/: page-level components
- services/: API calls
- hooks/: custom hooks

### State Management
- Use useState for local state
- Use useEffect for side effects
- Avoid deep prop drilling (use context if needed)

---

## TailwindCSS Rules
- Prefer utility classes over custom CSS
- Keep class order consistent:
  layout → spacing → size → color → effects
- Extract reusable UI components when repeated
- Avoid overly long class strings

---

## Backend (ExpressJS)

### Structure
- routes → controllers → services → models

### Rules
- Controllers handle request/response only
- Services contain business logic
- Do not write SQL in controllers
- Use async/await (no callbacks)

### API Response Format
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {}
}